{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-separates-orbits}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ed4c0ffd51411b4c2e632e1b91d2081be25503e0bad1f32bde8d4056062f0856", "source_text": "Follows immediately from Lemma <REF_0001> part (4).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:38727ebf3ed766ef8964e97b2d1a0db0992b1af00b209ef242f0b59b7d5c6404", "unit_id": "tag:049Z:proof"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$s, t$", "MATH_0002": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$U(k) \\to X(k)$", "MATH_0004": "$k$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:598968d451a89290d068045e4cb796f36849ccc97587715ce81185c4b42f99a9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:22396514f428f18732fa5bf78e897b98d21782934e0a993c1a74500c71b488b9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the following lemma it is (probably) not good enough to assume just that\nthe morphisms <MATH_0001> are locally of finite type. The reason is that\nit may happen that some map <MATH_0002> is an orbit space, yet is\nnot locally of finite type. In that case <MATH_0003> may not\nbe surjective for all algebraically closed fields <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a17a06e8605d7757e4bb24cd746e85e55870881069eb5f3a525b254ec7cc5e01", "unit_id": "tag:048M:prose-0012"}
